3 passed). I didn't run the rest of the suite or a linter (ruff isn't installed in the venv).\n\nThe router job came back as \"escalate\" because its final report had schema errors, but its own check run passed. I read the diff against the spec, found it matches, and merged the branch with `git merge --ff-only local-agent/j-20261016-c15eae`.\n\n- **`Loader.load` in `api.py`:** the new `Loader.substitute` raises `NotImplementedError` in the base class. `load` skips substitution for `SetEnv` types and when there is no `conf`, as the spec says.\n- **Subclasses:** `IniLoader` and `TomlLoader` each get their own `substitute`.\n- **Docs:** the new changelog file `docs/changelog/4047.bugfix.rst` and the \"Substitutions inside an override\" subsection in `docs/reference/config.rst` are in.\n\nThe worker also flagged that any other `Loader` subclass, such as the memory loader, would raise `NotImplementedError` if it ever received an override with a `conf`. That follows from the spec's \"base raises `NotImplementedError`\" and from other loaders being out of scope, so I left it.", "ttft_ms": 1963, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 86293, "uuid": "d0905ae4-1ec1-4211-860c-066403e34fc9", "ttft_stream_ms": 1149, "time_to_request_ms": 49, "first_content_frame_ms": 1153, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
